<title>USA: TABLE - FirstCity Q2 net decreases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - FirstCity Q2 net decreases.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended		  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>		June 30,	June 30,     June 30,	June 30,</p>
<p>		  1997	    1996	   1997	    1996</p>
<p>Net Gain on Purchased</p>
<p>Asset Pools</p>
<p>		 $4,891	  $3,952	$10,192	  $8,616</p>
<p>Gain on Sales of Mortgage Loans</p>
<p>		  8,407	   5,986	 15,283	  11,886</p>
<p>Provision for Loan Losses</p>
<p>		  1,357		--	  2,155		--</p>
<p>Provision (Benefit) for Income Taxes</p>
<p>		    229	(13,995)	    581	(12,952)</p>
<p>Net Earnings</p>
<p>		 $4,439	 $19,538	$13,656	 $24,196</p>
<p>Special Preferred Dividends</p>
<p>		  1,515	   1,938	  3,174	   3,876</p>
<p>Net Earnings to Common</p>
<p>		 $2,855	 $17,600	$10,413	 $20,320</p>
<p>Net Earnings Per Share</p>
<p>		  $0.44	   $2.71	  $1.60	   $3.12</p>
<p>Average Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>		  6,517	  6,502	  6,515	   6,502</p>
<p>		     (Amounts in Thousands Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  FirstCity Financial Corp said these results reflect its merger with Harbor Financial Group which was completed in July.</p>
<p>Net income for the first six months of 1997 included approximately $6.8 million, or $1.38 per share, of settlement proceeds derived from the first quarter termination of the investment management agreement with the FirstCity Liquidating Trust.</p>
<p>Net income for the first six months of 1996 included $2.97 in deferred tax benefits.</p>
<p>Net income was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
